    {
      "id": "F13",
      "statement": "What distinguishes the alerts. As fan-in indicators they look alike: 6–8 distinct senders in one event-time hour, one transfer per sender, no sender overlap and no shared sender devices. The recorded relationships beyond the indicator split them into three groups. (1) A-37573, A-83577 and A-10859 each have multi-link candidate onward paths (4, 5 and 3 links), whose first onward transfer comes soon after the credits. Each also has a device used by two or more accounts on its own route: D-45880 by four accounts, D-40018 by two non-adjacent accounts, D-79802 by two. (2) A-20636 and A-85921 each have a single 1-link path to one account, some contributing transfers with no link, and no shared device on the route. (3) A-28137 has no onward links and no route device sharing. This makes group (1) the clearest candidates for review; groups (2) and (3) show only the fan-in and timing. These relationships record timing and device use only. They do not show that the same funds moved, or establish fraud or common control.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "R1",
        "R2",
        "R3",
        "R4",
        "R5",
        "R6",
        "S1",
        "S2",
        "S3",
